prompt_template:
{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Field Guide. The recipient is a species. Every scene is a numbered plate with a caption and a margin note.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Motif from the strongest obsession or habitat fact (birds only if the facts point to birds). Binomial: genus from the name, species from a habit, in mock-Latin, with an English gloss underneath. Dryness follows {tone}: warm means 'observed with admiration', roasty means 'observed with concern'. Plate count equals scene count. With 3 photos or fewer, draw the rest; never leave a plate empty.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"binomial":"","gloss":"","edition":"","plate_titles":[""],"margin_note_voice":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Firmware. The card is a device that boots, profiles the recipient and runs diagnostics.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Device name from the recipient's name (NAME.EXE, NAME-OS, unit NAME-40). One module per fact, named from habits and obsessions. Version number from the age. Severity words follow {tone}. One flicker effect per scene at most, never on body text. Always include a skip-boot control.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"device_name":"","version":"","boot_lines":["x8"],"modules":[{"fact":"","label":"","status":""}],"warning_line":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Quest Log. The birthday is a quest chain and the recipient is the hero.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Class from the main hobby, as a pun (Barista of the North). Level equals age. Three to five stats from real traits, each a compliment with a twist. Inventory from objects and obsessions in the facts. The companion is the giver. World (fantasy, space, cosy) from what they love, not from their age. Rewards are badges and titles; never invent achievements about their real life.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"hero":{"name":"","class":"","level":0,"stats":[{"label":"","value":0}]},"inventory":[""],"companion":"","quests":[{"title":"","objective":"","reward":""}],"world":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Memory Box. The card is a box of keepsakes and each scene is one object.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Objects from real photos, places and dates in the facts. With fewer than 3 photos, design objects (tickets, recipe cards, maps) from facts instead of leaving gaps. The last object is always the giver's letter, unfolded last. Handwriting only for labels of 6 words or fewer. Accent from a fact if one exists. Never expose the letter in a share tile without separate approval.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"objects":[{"kind":"","label":"","fact":"","scene":0}],"lid_text":"","letter_object":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Technicolour. Every scene is a poster with one dominant graphic idea in a tight palette.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Giant numeral from the age or milestone. Palette from favourite colours in the facts, else from their mood: 3 to 4 colours only, and change composition, not colour, between scenes. 'Main character' title from their best-known trait. Taste profile from 4 to 6 favourite things. Each scene must also work as a standalone share tile.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"numeral":"","poster_titles":[""],"taste_tags":[""],"award":{"title":"","fact":""}}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Mixtape. Sections are tracks and the player is the navigation.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Medium from era and taste (cassette, vinyl or playlist screen; never assume a medium from age alone). One track title per scene from catchphrases, habits and memories, each with a made-up duration. J-card lettering from the giver's tone. 'Featuring' credits from voice notes or named friends. Never quote lyrics: songs are named by title only, and only if the giver named them.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"medium":"","side_a_title":"","side_b_title":"","tracks":[{"title":"","duration":"","scene":0}],"liner_notes":"","featuring":[""]}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Arcade Cabinet. An attract-mode arcade machine that ends on a high-score table.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Grid and colour limit from an era they loved, else 16 colours. 5 to 8 simple 16 by 16 sprites from favourite things, as rows of palette indexes a renderer can draw. Level titles from habits. Score is age x 1000 unless a joke number is in the facts. Three-letter initials for every named person, recipient first. Lives never run out. No third-party game characters, mazes or mechanics.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"grid":"","logo_text":"","levels":[{"title":"","sprite":"","scene":0}],"sprites":[{"name":"","rows":["16 strings"]}],"score":0,"high_scores":[{"initials":"","score":0}]}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Game Day. A broadcast and match programme with the recipient as the star player.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Sport from the facts; if none, invent one for their hobby (Competitive Napping). Position from their role in the group. Stats from habits, each with label, value and unit (coffees per game: 3.2). Roster from named friends, with jersey numbers from birthdays or jokes. Final score: the giver's side wins by the recipient's age, or a kind joke score. Invented teams and colours only: no real clubs, crests, leagues or players.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"sport":"","position":"","jersey":"","stats":[{"label":"","value":"","unit":""}],"roster":[{"name":"","number":""}],"ticker_lines":["x8"],"final_score":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Comic Book Issue. Each scene is a page of panels; captions and bubbles carry the text.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Character kit (hair, glasses, clothes, colour) only from appearance details the giver volunteered: never guess. Genre from tone: adventure, sci-fi, noir or slice-of-life. Origin story from a hobby or a memory. The sidekick is the giver. Issue number is the age or years known. Sound effects are original words. The last panel is 'to be continued' with a warm hook for next year. No known characters, costumes or logos.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"cover":{"title":"","issue":"","tagline":""},"character":{"parts":{"hair":"","glasses":"","top":"","colour":""}},"genre":"","pages":[{"layout":"","panels":[{"caption":"","bubble":"","sfx":""}]}],"next_issue":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Storybook. A picture book with the recipient as the hero.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Plot from a real milestone or hobby in the facts. Companion from a favourite animal or toy. Setting from a place they love. A refrain of 4 to 8 words that returns on every spread. At most 3 lines per spread, 8 words or fewer each for under 8s; rhyme only when it reads naturally. The hero is an original simple character built from volunteered details only. The giver appears as a helper. Never scary or sarcastic, and no teasing about body, behaviour or bedtime fights.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"title":"","refrain":"","hero":{"look":""},"companion":"","spreads":[{"layout":"","picture":"","lines":[""]}],"read_aloud":true}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Sticker Book. Each scene is a page and every fact is a die-cut sticker that reveals a short message.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: One sticker per fact, each with an icon described as a simple shape list, a label of 3 words or fewer and a hidden line of 12 words or fewer. Page count equals scene count, with 3 to 6 stickers per page (3 for under 8s). Backgrounds are plain, dotted, ruled or grid only. One sticker style per card. The final page has a star sticker signed by the giver. Nothing is required to finish: stickers can auto-place.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"pages":[{"background":"","stickers":[{"fact":"","icon":"","label":"","reveal":""}]}],"final_sticker":{"text":"","signed_by":""}}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Front Page. A newspaper about the recipient: a front page plus inside pages.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Paper name from a place or a joke (The Kettle Gazette). Dateline from the birthday and their town. Banner headline from the best-known trait or event, in straight news style. The giver is 'the editor' and named friends are correspondents. Choose 3 inside features from letters to the editor, classifieds, crossword, forecast, scoreboard. Every story is affectionate: no jokes about health, money, romance or death unless the facts say they are welcome. No real news events, outlets or journalists.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"paper_name":"","dateline":"","banner":"","standfirst":"","stories":[{"headline":"","byline":"","body":""}],"features":[{"kind":"","content":""}],"editor_note":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Premiere Night. The recipient stars in an invented feature and the giver is the director.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Genre from tone and personality. Title: a pun on the name or a habit. Tagline from a catchphrase. Cast from named friends with invented roles. One film-style title card per act, one scene per act. Era look from their taste. Credits list the giver, friends and pets. Invented titles, studios, awards and quotes only: no real films, actors, studios or lines.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"film_title":"","tagline":"","genre":"","cast":[{"name":"","role":""}],"acts":[{"card":"","scene":0}],"credits":[""],"post_credits":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Neon Night Drive. A synthwave night drive where each scene is a stop along the road.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Neon pair from favourite colours or the era they love. Station name from the recipient's name (NAME FM). One billboard per scene from catchphrases or places. Vehicle silhouette from their real vehicle or hobby, in original shapes with no real models. 'Now playing' lists track titles only, never lyrics. Text sits on solid panels; glow is for shapes and headings only. Cut road motion when reduced-motion is on.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"station":"","vehicle":"","billboards":[{"text":"","scene":0}],"now_playing":[""],"horizon":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Blueprint. The recipient is drawn as a well-engineered assembly on technical drawing sheets.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Assembly from a hobby or tool (a bicycle for a cyclist). Parts from real traits, each numbered with a note in technical voice. Tolerances from habits (Tolerance: plus or minus 10 minutes on arrival). Title block: drawn by the giver, checked by friends, revision equal to the age. Discipline from their work or hobby. Drawings are simple SVG parts, never traced photos. At least one note per sheet says what the recipient does well.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"assembly":"","sheets":[{"title":"","scale":"","parts":[{"n":1,"label":"","note":""}]}],"title_block":{"drawn_by":"","checked_by":"","revision":""},"revision_table":[{"rev":"","note":""}]}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Passport. A travel passport and journal where each scene is a destination.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Destinations from real places in the facts (where they lived, met, holidayed, dream of), in story order. Invent 'places' only for habits and mark them as jokes (Snack Cove). Visa categories from habits. 'Valid for' equals the age. Style from their travel taste. Departure and arrival cards use the birthday date. No real airline, airport or visa-authority logos, and no layouts that could pass as an official document.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"cover":{"country":"","holder":"","valid_for":""},"stops":[{"place":"","stamp_text":"","postcard":"","scene":0}],"visas":[""],"arrival":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Carnival Midway. A night fairground where each scene is a booth and the prizes are the messages.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Booth names from habits and obsessions (Coffee Toss). The barker is the giver. A height-sign joke from the age. Stripes from favourite colours. Games are gentle, skippable and always won; prizes are messages or badges. Finale: the top of the Ferris wheel with the real message. No scary clowns and no side-show jokes about bodies.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"gate_ticket":"","booths":[{"name":"","game":"","prize":"","scene":0}],"barker_voice":"","finale":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Case File. An affectionate investigation of a 'person of interest'.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Case number from the birth date. 'Suspicious activities' from habits, each with an evidence tag. Witness quotes from catchphrases and named friends. Redaction bars hide a kind twist, never something hurtful. Tone (noir, procedural or cosy mystery) follows {tone}. The verdict is guilty of something lovable. No real agencies, forces, badges or seals, and no offence that could read as real: keep every charge comic and harmless.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"case_number":"","subject":"","charges":[{"label":"","evidence":""}],"witnesses":[{"name":"","statement":""}],"redactions":[{"line":"","reveal":""}],"verdict":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Gallery Wall. A small museum show where the recipient's life is the collection.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Exhibition title from the name and the span of years. Rooms by decade or by theme, whichever the facts support. Pieces from photos, objects, quotes and habits, each with a title, year, medium ('coffee on paper') and one warm line. The curator is the giver. Voice is reverent or wry per {tone}. Fill gaps with designed objects, never empty frames. No imitation of real artworks, artists or museums. Finish at a visitors' book.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"exhibition":{"title":"","subtitle":"","curator":""},"rooms":[{"title":"","pieces":[{"title":"","year":"","medium":"","label":"","fact":""}],"scene":0}],"visitors_book":""}

{THEME_PREAMBLE}
THEME: Café Menu. A tasting menu in the recipient's honour where each scene is a course.
KIT: {KIT}
DERIVE: Menu style from what they love, never from assumptions about their background. Dish names from memories and habits; a real food or drink is named only if the facts mention it. Courses in order: amuse-bouche (opener), starter, main, palate cleanser (a game), dessert (the heartfelt part), digestif (sign-off). Prices are jokes ('priceless', 'three coffees'). The bill reads 'paid in full by everyone who loves you'. Pairings use only drinks the facts mention; alcohol only if the facts say so and never for under 18s. No real restaurants, chefs or brands.
OUTPUT: {THEME_JSON} + {"menu_title":"","style":"","courses":[{"course":"","dish":"","description":"","tasting_note":"","scene":0}],"specials":[""],"bill":{"lines":[{"item":"","price":""}],"total":""}}
